@fm description | description | How flour, butter and sacks are received at the back door of Crumbwick Bakery.
# Deliveries
s description | Deliveries arrive between six and eight on Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday.
s description | The flour driver is called Odalys and the butter driver is called Fenn.
## Receiving
s gate{del_count} | Count the sacks at the back door before you sign the driver's sheet.
s rule | Check the date on each butter block.
s gate{del_sign} | Sign the driver's sheet only after the count matches the sheet.
s prohibition{del_leave} | Never let a driver leave sacks outside the back door.
s example | For example, a sack of tarn flour left in the rain on a Saturday had to be thrown away.
## Storing
l rule{del_flour} | Put new flour sacks behind the old ones in the flour store
l rule | Stand butter blocks in the cold room on the middle shelf
l prohibition | Do not stack flour sacks higher than four
l description | The flour store is the dry room next to the back door
l example | A stack of five sacks on the left wall tipped over last winter and split three of them
## Problems
s rule | Phone the supplier if a sack is torn or a butter block is soft.
s gate | Take a photo of a damaged sack before you move it.
s prohibition{del_torn} | Do not use flour from a torn sack in the dough.
s description | A torn sack may let in damp and insects.
s example | Case: flour from a torn sack went into a batch on a Thursday and the whole batch was binned.
## Paperwork
s rule | Hand the signed sheet to the shop manager by noon.
s description | The shop manager files each sheet in the grey box.
s rule | Greet the drivers with a smile.
